WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.000
What do you do

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:03.040
before you shoot a scene
to get into...

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:05.480
I just drink juice and
eat food. I don't really...

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:07.640
I don't really--
I don't know man.

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:09.120
I don't think about it much.

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:10.600
You're just
naturally talented.

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:11.640
He's a natural.

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:13.320
When you think about it,

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.320
that's when things
start to go wrong.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:17.320
I don't learn lines
on purpose.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:18.320
Bun that.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:42.280
So, this season,
you're not only an actor,

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:45.440
you're also an EP,
an executive producer.

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:48.720
So, what does that mean?
What do you do as an exec?

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:50.360
It means
I can write you out.

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:53.840
That's what it means.

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:56.920
It means...

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.600
D'you know what,
it means empowerment...

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:02.760
for us

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:06.120
because we can have
some, you know, impact

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:09.280
on the stories
that are gonna to be told

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:12.480
about the lives
that most of us on this...

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:13.360
D'you know what I mean,

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:16.120
on this platform have led,
d'you know what I'm saying?

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:17.520
You know,
the beauty of Top Boy is

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:20.160
that it represents
a certain people.

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:25.760
And I know myself 100%,
and Kane,

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:29.040
have come from that life,
d'you know what I'm saying?

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:31.080
So, who better
to tell those stories

00:01:31.160 --> 00:01:32.960
or be a part
of shaping those stories

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:34.920
for the rest of the world
to see?

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:38.280
You know, we've been
involved in the scripts,

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:39.520
we've been involved

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:41.680
in like the journey
of you lot's characters,

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:44.920
not only our own characters
but kinda where you guys go.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:46.680
It's good to have
that position,

00:01:46.760 --> 00:01:48.120
it's good to be able to...

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:51.280
to just be a bit
more involved creatively

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:52.840
in what happens
with the show.

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:56.000
I got a link

00:01:56.080 --> 00:01:57.360
to Spain and Morocco.

00:01:58.160 --> 00:01:59.880
About to come through
with a big bit.

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:05.360
More money than you've seen
in your life, bro.

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:09.280
Do you wanna be a part of it
or what?

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:10.960
Part of it how?

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:13.040
By doing
what you always done.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:15.200
Selling food.

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:16.440
Your food, yeah?

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:19.800
I guess it is, yeah.
My food.

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:22.120
From the first season,

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:25.120
that's when
I really wanted to be in it.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:27.600
I saw Dris,
we were from the same...

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:29.720
How old were you then?

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:34.120
-Probably 14, 15.
-OK.

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:35.480
I see Dris in the show.

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:37.480
We're from the same area,
so I was like,

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:39.800
"Bro, you can't get man
in the show? Bro..."

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:42.920
Didn't really
work like that.

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:43.880
D'you know what I'm saying.

00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:45.480
But then I heard
they were doing auditions

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:47.280
for the next season
that was coming.

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:49.160
I see one of my guys pull up
with his cousin,

00:02:49.240 --> 00:02:50.880
his cousin's an actor,
he had an agent at the time,

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:51.760
everything.

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:54.120
I see him
just walking past all of us,

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:55.560
doing his thing and cut.

00:02:55.640 --> 00:02:58.720
I was thinking: Is that
the power of an agent?

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:01.680
I need to find a way to get
an agent or something.

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:03.680
I didn't even
get to do the audition.

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:05.560
And then this time
came around...

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:07.280
Remember my cousin
telling me

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:08.320
she was like
yeah she heard

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:09.800
that there's
auditions for Top Boy

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:11.120
and I was like, "You sure?"

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:12.600
She said yeah,
so, I asked my agent

00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:14.120
to keep her ears open.

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:15.800
She was like,
"I suggested you for it."

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:17.520
I was like, "Yeah?

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:20.360
A'ight. OK. Say no more",

00:03:20.440 --> 00:03:22.440
you know what I'm sayin',
and then, yeah.

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:25.320
Today, there's so many
different routes to market.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:28.080
Back in the day, you talked
about the agent thing,

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:31.000
it had to be an agent thing,
you had to have an agent.

00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:33.640
"How do I get an agent
if I haven't done anything."

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:35.200
The answer was,
"I don't know".

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:36.640
You know, one of them ones.

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:40.640
But now, with the rise
in social media,

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:42.920
where people
like Des street casting,

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:44.560
there are
many different avenues

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:45.520
into the game.

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:48.560
I told some of my friends,

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:50.440
"You don't have to go
to drama school,

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:53.200
you don't have to have...",
you know?

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:55.920
You can do it yourself,
you can set up your camera

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:58.240
and learn a monologue
and record it yourself,

00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:00.960
hit up an agency on a DM,
send it to them.

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:02.560
Shoot your shot.

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:04.440
We've had
some interesting stories

00:04:04.520 --> 00:04:06.240
of how people
have got into the show

00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:09.680
and I wanna hear yours
'cause I know you...

00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:11.400
I heard

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:13.960
there was something to do
with a barber shop.

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:15.320
Yeah.

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:19.080
So, I remember
I was going back to school

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:21.400
and my hair was
just horrendous.

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:23.160
I'm in the barbers
and the barber

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:25.520
is doing some madness
to people's hair.

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:28.080
I'm seeing zig zags,
people's hairlines are back,

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:30.360
I'm thinking:
Yeah, you need to get out

00:04:30.440 --> 00:04:32.640
because this is not it.

00:04:32.720 --> 00:04:35.400
So, then,
as I was about to leave,

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:39.600
a woman came to us and said,
"Audition for Top Boy".

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:42.440
At first, I was thinking
she's not telling the truth,

00:04:42.520 --> 00:04:43.520
she's just chatting

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:46.200
because Top Boy,
that's a long time ago,

00:04:46.280 --> 00:04:47.320
so what's going on?

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:49.680
But then she was like,
"No, it's real.

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:52.200
I'll just write your name
down in my book

00:04:52.280 --> 00:04:53.320
and I'll give you
a certain time

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:55.520
to come in
to a certain place."

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:57.600
I was like, "I might as well

00:04:57.680 --> 00:04:59.240
'cause
I have nothing to do."

00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:02.200
I went in and then, yeah...

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:05.320
The rest is history.
You're here.

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:08.600
So, I love those stories,
man.

00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:10.360
Like, they touch me, man.

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:22.880
This season especially

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:26.440
has given
such an incredible platform

00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:28.960
for all the female cast

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:32.800
to have
these dimensional characters

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:34.400
that have so much to them.

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:37.920
From the last season,
Lauryn starts off like,

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:40.800
"Ha ha, champagne, boys!",
all of that.

00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:42.560
And then, towards the end,

00:05:42.640 --> 00:05:44.840
it all goes terribly wrong
for her.

00:05:44.920 --> 00:05:46.600
But I feel like this season,

00:05:46.680 --> 00:05:50.520
it's just a series
of unfortunate events

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:51.760
again and again.

00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:55.600
And the subject matter
and the storyline

00:05:55.680 --> 00:05:57.960
was not something
I took lightly at all.

00:05:58.040 --> 00:06:02.880
It was kind of interesting,
we were half filming Top Boy

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:04.360
during the pandemic,

00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:08.160
domestic violence was
at an all-time high.

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:09.920
So, I actually
got in contact

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:12.320
with
a domestic violence charity

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:16.720
in order to speak to them
and help me navigate

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:18.680
how to, you know...

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:22.200
tell the truth
with my character

00:06:22.280 --> 00:06:23.560
and what she goes through.

00:06:23.640 --> 00:06:26.600
Curtis, please.
Can I have some privacy?

00:06:26.680 --> 00:06:29.400
I'm only going in there
to try some things on.

00:06:30.440 --> 00:06:31.880
Please.

00:06:31.960 --> 00:06:33.440
No, she's right.

00:06:33.520 --> 00:06:35.120
She needs her privacy.

00:06:36.840 --> 00:06:37.760
Thank you.

00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:39.400
I'll go with her.

00:06:39.480 --> 00:06:41.400
Oh, yeah. Go on.

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:46.800
Come here.

00:06:47.480 --> 00:06:49.720
What's wrong?
Baby, what's wrong?

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:54.320
Please, please,
I'm just so ashamed.

00:06:54.400 --> 00:06:57.680
Look, I feel so ugly
and bloated

00:06:57.760 --> 00:06:59.880
and I don't want anyone
seeing me like this.

00:06:59.960 --> 00:07:03.560
It's only Vee.
Eh, you're beautiful to me.

00:07:03.640 --> 00:07:04.840
To me?

00:07:04.920 --> 00:07:07.640
-Did you just say that?
-What I meant was you're...

00:07:07.720 --> 00:07:09.440
-What, I disgust you? Yeah?
-No.

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:11.360
Come here, come here.

00:07:11.920 --> 00:07:12.920
Hey, it's all right.

00:07:13.520 --> 00:07:15.080
Can I please be by myself?

00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:18.960
-One minute, please?
-All right, just don't cry.

00:07:19.760 --> 00:07:20.920
You go.

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:32.000
Please
can I have some money?

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:34.560
Although I've come
from a different background

00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:35.680
to the characters
in the story,

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:39.120
I've been given
such an amazing storyline.

00:07:39.200 --> 00:07:41.600
As someone
who came into the show

00:07:41.680 --> 00:07:43.360
as a new person,

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:44.960
it showed me
for the first time

00:07:45.040 --> 00:07:46.640
that it was a possibility

00:07:46.720 --> 00:07:49.240
that I could be
in something like that.

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:50.120
To be honest,

00:07:50.200 --> 00:07:52.440
the whole experience
was quite nerve-wracking.

00:07:53.080 --> 00:07:55.960
I mean, I'm so lucky
that I had Saffron and Jazz.

00:07:56.040 --> 00:07:59.120
Like,
they were so supportive.

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:01.160
Saffron,
we had loads of bants,

00:08:01.240 --> 00:08:02.280
we had so many LOLs.

00:08:02.360 --> 00:08:04.000
-Constant laughing.
-Yeah.

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:07.240
One of my first scenes was
kind of like a mad scene

00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:08.520
that was so challenging.

00:08:08.600 --> 00:08:10.800
I didn't really understand
any of the language,

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:14.720
it was so new to me to be,
like, in front of the camera

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:15.880
in such a different way.

00:08:15.960 --> 00:08:17.040
It's so interesting,

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:21.000
you can do as many
acting classes as you want,

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:22.720
you can train
as much as you want

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:24.280
when you're at home,

00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:27.000
but, actually,
being on set is the lesson.

00:08:27.080 --> 00:08:28.680
I like your style.

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:32.680
It's not my style,
it's just me.

00:08:33.440 --> 00:08:35.600
OK, well, I like you.

00:08:36.960 --> 00:08:38.400
I think
you look really great.

00:08:42.600 --> 00:08:43.560
That was your cue...

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:47.920
to say something
really nice,

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:50.560
preferably without me
having to prompt you.

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:56.440
I mean,

00:08:56.520 --> 00:08:58.840
when Li said to me
she wanted to hook me up,

00:08:58.920 --> 00:09:02.000
I wasn't expecting her
to look like you.

00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:04.520
What's it like
being recognised

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:05.560
in the show?

00:09:06.960 --> 00:09:10.000
Like, doing your own thing,
you're still at school.

00:09:10.080 --> 00:09:11.400
Are girls running after you?

00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:13.560
-No. No girls.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:09:14.200 --> 00:09:16.440
I think, in general,
I still live a normal life

00:09:16.520 --> 00:09:18.240
'cause I still live
with my mum.

00:09:18.760 --> 00:09:20.160
However,
I am more recognised

00:09:20.240 --> 00:09:21.880
in certain places
which I go.

00:09:21.960 --> 00:09:23.560
More doors are open for me,

00:09:23.640 --> 00:09:24.760
but, in general,

00:09:24.840 --> 00:09:27.720
I try to keep to myself,
quiet,

00:09:27.800 --> 00:09:29.720
and to focus on
what I need to do.

00:09:29.800 --> 00:09:32.160
No, I saw you filming
a music video

00:09:32.240 --> 00:09:33.600
in the middle of Shoreditch,

00:09:33.680 --> 00:09:36.000
so I don't know
what you're talking about!

00:09:36.080 --> 00:09:38.320
When you were there
like, "Ay".

00:09:38.400 --> 00:09:41.520
I was like, "Is that Aaron?"
and you said, "You cool?"

00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:43.200
and then
you went back to it.

00:09:43.280 --> 00:09:46.520
No, that was my friend
who I was supporting.

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:47.840
-Yeah...
-But I think...

00:09:49.160 --> 00:09:52.280
No, but, in general,
I do like to keep quiet

00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:56.000
and just perfect
the art of acting, so...

00:09:56.080 --> 00:10:01.040
In sixth form, I'm at home
trying to work on my accent

00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:02.640
or doing auditions.

00:10:02.720 --> 00:10:06.240
Looking back
on your Top Boy legacy,

00:10:06.320 --> 00:10:08.360
what does all that
mean to you?

00:10:08.440 --> 00:10:10.560
How does it feel
to be sat here today?

00:10:10.640 --> 00:10:11.960
When we started this thing,

00:10:12.040 --> 00:10:15.600
we didn't even know
it was gonna get made.

00:10:15.680 --> 00:10:17.280
When I read
those first scripts

00:10:17.360 --> 00:10:18.480
that Ronan wrote

00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:20.680
and I see people
getting shot in their head

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:22.960
and fingers getting cut off
and all this stuff,

00:10:23.040 --> 00:10:25.680
that stuff
had never been on TV before.

00:10:25.760 --> 00:10:28.080
This life,
the story of this life

00:10:28.160 --> 00:10:29.480
had never been told

00:10:29.560 --> 00:10:31.200
in the way
that it was about to be told

00:10:31.280 --> 00:10:32.040
at that moment.

00:10:32.120 --> 00:10:35.360
Me and Kane would be on set
shooting scenes,

00:10:35.440 --> 00:10:36.600
night shoots,

00:10:36.680 --> 00:10:38.560
doing these crazy things,

00:10:38.640 --> 00:10:41.080
actually looking
at each other feeling like:

00:10:41.800 --> 00:10:43.600
Is this actually
going to get put out?

00:10:43.680 --> 00:10:44.960
Are we wasting our time?

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:47.120
Are they gonna put this
on TV?

00:10:47.600 --> 00:10:49.320
And to see
what it's grown into,

00:10:49.400 --> 00:10:51.960
there was no point
where we sat there thinking:

00:10:52.040 --> 00:10:54.440
This is going to be huge,
know what I'm sayin'?

00:10:54.520 --> 00:10:56.880
We just didn't know
what the beast would be.

00:10:56.960 --> 00:10:59.000
So, to be able
to sit back now,

00:10:59.080 --> 00:11:01.440
see it on Netflix,

00:11:01.520 --> 00:11:04.920
see it doing well
in the States and Europe.

00:11:05.000 --> 00:11:07.440
-Billboards...
-Billboards and whatever.

00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:08.400
Times Square.

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:11.800
Yeah. It's like...
It was no easy thing.

00:11:11.880 --> 00:11:14.400
Why do you think Top Boy is
still relevant today?

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:19.920
I think it's relevant
'cause it depicts real life.

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:21.120
There's actually youths

00:11:21.200 --> 00:11:24.840
that come
from a deprived community

00:11:25.560 --> 00:11:28.280
that go through
these real-life situations.

00:11:28.360 --> 00:11:30.320
It's important
that these stories are told

00:11:30.400 --> 00:11:33.280
so people can get an insight
of how it actually is.

00:11:33.360 --> 00:11:37.080
It's not senseless in a way,

00:11:37.160 --> 00:11:38.840
everyone's doing something
for a reason,

00:11:38.920 --> 00:11:40.680
everyone's trying to live
and survive,

00:11:40.760 --> 00:11:44.040
everyone wants
a better life.

00:11:48.280 --> 00:11:50.320
People thought
I was a wasteman

00:11:50.400 --> 00:11:52.560
on the last one because
I missed with the shotgun.

00:11:53.920 --> 00:11:56.320
Were you getting challenged
about that?

00:11:56.400 --> 00:11:58.320
Everywhere I'd go,
"How could you let him

00:11:58.400 --> 00:11:59.760
overpower you
with the shotgun?"

00:11:59.840 --> 00:12:00.920
Yeah.

